# Nature's Lore searches its controller's library for a Forest card - basic or not (CR 109.2, 205.3i, 701.23b) - and puts it
# onto the battlefield, then shuffles (CR 701.23, 701.24). Bot1's library holds Temple Garden (a Forest though
# nonbasic and also a Plains) and a Forest: the search refuses an Island, takes the Garden, and Bot1 pays 2 life for
# its entry so it arrives untapped. Bot2's Forest stays in its hand: only your own library is searched.

[Bot1 Deck]
Nature's Lore
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Island
Island
Island
Island
Temple Garden
Forest
Island x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Nature's Lore.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
! Bot1.Search(Island)
! Bot1.Search(Temple Garden; Forest)
Bot1.Search(Temple Garden)
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 1
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot1.Battlefield.Temple Garden.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 3
Bot1.Hand.Count = 4
Bot1.Library.Count = 12
Bot1.Graveyard = Nature's Lore
Bot2.Hand.Count = 7
Bot2.Library.Count = 13
Bot1.Shuffles = 1
